# -*- encoding: utf-8 -*-
# Arc: VargaMarionPath | Scene: MarionPath3

translate pt strings:

    old "Sarah woke the next day."
    new "Sarah acordou no dia seguinte."

    old "Except for herself, the bed was empty."
    new "Com exceção dela mesma, a cama estava vazia."

    old "Light was already creeping through the curtains."
    new "A luz já se infiltrava pelas cortinas."

    old "What time was it?"
    new "Que horas eram?"

    old "She wondered where Marion could be. Likely busy, as he always appeared to be."
    new "Ela se perguntava onde Marion poderia estar. Provavelmente ocupado, como ele sempre parecia estar."

    old "Sarah couldn't blame him."
    new "Sarah não podia culpá-lo."

    old "There was a lot of work to be done."
    new "Havia muito trabalho a ser feito."

    old "They had defeated the Tribes, but victory was not so clean."
    new "Eles haviam derrotado as Tribos, mas a vitória não foi tão limpa assim."

    old "Endless reports had begun to make their way to the capital, petitions urging Thomas to act."
    new "Relatórios intermináveis já haviam começado a chegar à capital, com petições exigindo que Thomas agisse."

    old "For while the Capital had managed to repel the Tribes and break their army, the Eastern Provinces had not been so fortunate."
    new "Pois, embora a Capital tivesse conseguido repelir as Tribos e destruir seu exército, as Províncias Orientais não tiveram a mesma sorte."

    old "Many towns had been raided, pillaged, burned."
    new "Muitas cidades haviam sido saqueadas, pilhadas e incendiadas."

    old "Reports told of entire towns, sometimes even cities, ruined."
    new "Os relatórios falavam de cidades inteiras, por vezes até mesmo metrópoles, reduzidas a ruínas."

    old "Worse still, scouts often spoke of how few bodies they actually discovered among the ruins."
    new "Pior ainda, os batedores muitas vezes relatavam o quão poucos corpos eles realmente encontravam entre as ruínas."

    old "If a city was burned, one expected countless dead."
    new "Se uma cidade era incendiada, esperava-se encontrar inúmeros mortos."

    old "Without the bodies, there was only one other troubling truth."
    new "Sem os corpos, havia apenas outra verdade preocupante."

    old "Many of the inhabitants of the Eastern Provinces had suffered slavery at the hands of the Tribes."
    new "Muitos dos habitantes das Províncias Orientais haviam sofrido escravidão nas mãos das Tribos."

    old "Some had been freed, after the battle outside the Capital, but many were not accounted for."
    new "Alguns haviam sido libertados após a batalha fora da Capital, mas muitos não foram encontrados."

    old "Sons. Daughters. Wives. Carried off in chains to Gods knew where."
    new "Filhos. Filhas. Esposas. Levados em correntes para sabe-se lá onde."

    old "Their farms, burned. Their cattle, killed and left to rot in the sun."
    new "Suas fazendas, queimadas. Seu gado, morto e deixado para apodrecer sob o sol."

    old "Those who had managed to escape the Tribes, had found their homes gone."
    new "Aqueles que conseguiram escapar das Tribos descobriram que suas casas haviam desaparecido."

    old "They still had their lives, but such things were cheap when one had no money, family or home."
    new "Eles ainda tinham suas vidas, mas tais coisas eram baratas quando se não se tinha dinheiro, família ou lar."

    old "Some of these men and women had been farmers for generations, reaching back beyond even their grandparents."
    new "Alguns desses homens e mulheres eram agricultores há gerações, uma tradição que remontava até antes de seus avós."

    old "All the certainty of their lives had been wiped away."
    new "Toda a certeza de suas vidas havia sido apagada."

    old "The cities of Rosanna were swelling with refugees."
    new "As cidades de Rosanna estavam se enchendo de refugiados."

    old "And as was so often the case, those who still had something, resented and feared those who now had nothing."
    new "E, como acontecia com tanta frequência, aqueles que ainda tinham algo ressentiam e temiam aqueles que agora não tinham mais nada."

    old "For in them, they saw their own worst fears reflected."
    new "Pois neles, eles viam refletidos os seus próprios piores medos."

    old "That they were not all so different, and that they likewise lived upon the edge between surviving and ruin."
    new "Que eles não eram tão diferentes assim, e que também viviam no limite entre a sobrevivência e a ruína."
